      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "To find \\(ab + ac + bc\\), where \\(a\\), \\(b\\), and \\(c\\) are the roots of the polynomial \\(3x^3 - 3x^2 + 11x - 8 = 0\\), we can use Vieta's formulas. Vieta's formulas relate the coefficients of a polynomial to sums and products of its roots. For a cubic polynomial of the form \\(ax^3 + bx^2 + cx + d = 0\\), the formulas are:\n\n1. \\(a + b + c = -\\frac{b}{a}\\)\n2. \\(ab + ac + bc = \\frac{c}{a}\\)\n3. \\(abc = -\\frac{d}{a}\\)\n\nGiven the polynomial \\(3x^3 - 3x^2 + 11x - 8 = 0\\), we have \\(a = 3\\), \\(b = -3\\), \\(c = 11\\), and \\(d = -8\\).\n\nFirst, we calculate \\(a + b + c\\):\n\\[\na + b + c = -\\frac{b}{a} = -\\frac{-3}{3} = 1\n\\]\n\nNext, we calculate \\(ab + ac + bc\\):\n\\[\nab + ac + bc = \\frac{c}{a} = \\frac{11}{3}\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the value of \\(ab + ac + bc\\) is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\frac{11}{3}}\n\\]",
